# WS2-06. # Sources: spec/16-borrow-rules.md BR-2/BR-3/BR-4 (a live loan blocks mutation, a second writable loan, or a move of the owner) and spec/appendix-stdlib.md §3 ("While any element view is live, push, reserve, and set are E10031 or E10032"); a loan is live only until its last use (NLL v2, spec/16).
The view is used only on the then-branch; the else-branch mutation
# is outside the loan.
profiles: host
with: tok.clo
expect: output
contrast: xs.push(5);\n        println($"{xs.len()}"); ==> xs.push(5);\n        println($"{v[0]}");
contrast-expect: reject E10031
--- output
1
2
